---@field modified_on? string|distilled.Null
---@field name? string|distilled.Null A unique name to identify the waiting room. Only alphanumeric characters, hyphens and underscores are allowed.
---@field new_users_per_minute? number|distilled.Null Sets the number of new users that will be let into the route every minute. This value is used as baseline for the number of users that are let in per minute. So it is possible that there is a little more or little less traffic coming to the route based on the traffic patterns at that time around the world.
---@field next_event_prequeue_start_time? string|distilled.Null An ISO 8601 timestamp that marks when the next event will begin queueing.
---@field next_event_start_time? string|distilled.Null An ISO 8601 timestamp that marks when the next event will start.
---@field path? string|distilled.Null Sets the path within the host to enable the waiting room on. The waiting room will be enabled for all subpaths as well. If there are two waiting rooms on the same subpath, the waiting room for the most specific path will be chosen. Wildcards and query parameters are not supported.
---@field queue_all? boolean|distilled.Null If queue_all is `true`, all the traffic that is coming to a route will be sent to the waiting room. No new traffic can get to the route once this field is set and estimated time will become unavailable.
---@field queueing_method? cloudflare.waiting_rooms.GetResponseQueueingMethod|distilled.Null Sets the queueing method used by the waiting room. Changing this parameter from the **default** queueing method is only available for the Waiting Room Advanced subscription. Regardless of the queueing method, if `queue_all` is enabled or an event is prequeueing, users in the waiting room will not be accepted to the origin. These users will always see a waiting room page that refreshes automatically. The valid queueing methods are:
---@field queueing_status_code? cloudflare.waiting_rooms.GetResponseQueueingStatusCode|distilled.Null HTTP status code returned to a user while in the queue.
---@field session_duration? number|distilled.Null Lifetime of a cookie (in minutes) set by Cloudflare for users who get access to the route. If a user is not seen by Cloudflare again in that time period, they will be treated as a new user that visits the route.
---@field suspended? boolean|distilled.Null Suspends or allows traffic going to the waiting room. If set to `true`, the traffic will not go to the waiting room.
---@field total_active_users? number|distilled.Null Sets the total number of active user sessions on the route at a point in time. A route is a combination of host and path on which a waiting room is available. This value is used as a baseline for the total number of active user sessions on the route. It is possible to have a situation where there are more or less active users sessions on the route based on the traffic patterns at that time around the world.
---@field turnstile_action? cloudflare.waiting_rooms.GetResponseTurnstileAction|distilled.Null Which action to take when a bot is detected using Turnstile. `log` will have no impact on queueing behavior, simply keeping track of how many bots are detected in Waiting Room Analytics. `infinite_queue` will send bots to a false queueing state, where they will never reach your origin. `infinite_queue` requires Advanced Waiting Room.
---@field turnstile_mode? cloudflare.waiting_rooms.GetResponseTurnstileMode|distilled.Null Which Turnstile widget type to use for detecting bot traffic. See [the Turnstile documentation](https://developers.cloudflare.com/turnstile/concepts/widget/#widget-types) for the definitions of these widget types. Set to `off` to disable the Turnstile integration entirely. Setting this to anything other than `off` or `invisible` requires Advanced Waiting Room.

