---@field event_start_time string An ISO 8601 timestamp that marks the start of the event. At this time, queued users will be processed with the event's configuration. The start time must be at least one minute before `event_end_time`.
---@field name string A unique name to identify the event. Only alphanumeric characters, hyphens and underscores are allowed.
---@field custom_page_html? string If set, the event will override the waiting room's `custom_page_html` property while it is active. If null, the event will inherit it.
---@field description? string A note that you can use to add more details about the event.
---@field disable_session_renewal? boolean If set, the event will override the waiting room's `disable_session_renewal` property while it is active. If null, the event will inherit it.
---@field new_users_per_minute? number If set, the event will override the waiting room's `new_users_per_minute` property while it is active. If null, the event will inherit it. This can only be set if the event's `total_active_users` property is also set.
---@field prequeue_start_time? string An ISO 8601 timestamp that marks when to begin queueing all users before the event starts. The prequeue must start at least five minutes before `event_start_time`.
---@field queueing_method? string If set, the event will override the waiting room's `queueing_method` property while it is active. If null, the event will inherit it.
---@field session_duration? number If set, the event will override the waiting room's `session_duration` property while it is active. If null, the event will inherit it.
---@field shuffle_at_event_start? boolean If enabled, users in the prequeue will be shuffled randomly at the `event_start_time`. Requires that `prequeue_start_time` is not null. This is useful for situations when many users will join the event prequeue at the same time and you want to shuffle them to ensure fairness. Naturally, it makes the most sense to enable this feature when the `queueing_method` during the event respects ordering such as **fifo**, or else the shuffling may be unnecessary.
---@field suspended? boolean Suspends or allows an event. If set to `true`, the event is ignored and traffic will be handled based on the waiting room configuration.
---@field total_active_users? number If set, the event will override the waiting room's `total_active_users` property while it is active. If null, the event will inherit it. This can only be set if the event's `new_users_per_minute` property is also set.
---@field turnstile_action? cloudflare.waiting_rooms.EventsEditRequestTurnstileAction|string If set, the event will override the waiting room's `turnstile_action` property while it is active. If null, the event will inherit it.
---@field turnstile_mode? cloudflare.waiting_rooms.EventsEditRequestTurnstileMode|string If set, the event will override the waiting room's `turnstile_mode` property while it is active. If null, the event will inherit it.

